    "readme_description": "Given an `m x n` `picture` consisting of black `'B'` and white `'W'` pixels, return the number of **black** lonely pixels.\n\nA black lonely pixel is a character `'B'` located at a specific position where the same row and same column don't have **any other** black pixels.",
